# Version Control
Rule Type: Always

## Commit Rules
### Message Format
- Format: "type(scope): description"
- Types:
  - feat: New feature
  - fix: Bug fix
  - docs: Documentation
  - style: Code style
  - refactor: Code refactoring
  - test: Testing
  - chore: Maintenance

### Commit Requirements
- Atomic commits
- Descriptive messages
- Reference issues
- Include scope
- Follow format

## Branch Strategy
### Branch Types
- feature: New features
- bugfix: Bug fixes
- hotfix: Urgent fixes
- release: Release preparation

### Branch Naming
- Format: "type/description"
- Examples:
  - feature/add-stop-loss
  - bugfix/fix-signal-generation
  - hotfix/fix-order-execution
  - release/v1.0.0

## Workflow
### Feature Development
- Create feature branch
- Develop feature
- Write tests
- Update documentation
- Create pull request

### Bug Fixes
- Create bugfix branch
- Fix bug
- Add tests
- Update documentation
- Create pull request

### Releases
- Create release branch
- Version bump
- Update changelog
- Tag release
- Merge to main

## Code Review
### Pull Request Requirements
- Descriptive title
- Detailed description
- Reference issues
- Include tests
- Update documentation

### Review Process
- Code review
- Test review
- Documentation review
- Performance review
- Security review

## Versioning
### Semantic Versioning
- Major: Breaking changes
- Minor: New features
- Patch: Bug fixes
- Pre-release: Alpha/Beta
- Build metadata

### Version Management
- Tag releases
- Update version
- Maintain changelog
- Document changes
- Track dependencies

## Maintenance
### Branch Maintenance
- Delete merged branches
- Update main branch
- Clean old branches
- Archive releases
- Maintain history

### Repository Maintenance
- Regular cleanup
- Update .gitignore
- Maintain hooks
- Review permissions
- Backup repository

## Documentation
### Version Documentation
- Update changelog
- Document releases
- Track dependencies
- Note breaking changes
- Include migration guides

### Process Documentation
- Document workflow
- Update guidelines
- Maintain templates
- Track changes
- Review regularly
